# Trivy vulnerability ignore file for docker-validate.yml's container-image scan
# (.github/workflows/docker-validate.yml, "Scan container images for vulnerabilities" step).
#
# Same convention as scripts/ops/db-cve-allowlist.txt: only for CVEs with no non-breaking fix
# available to this project (upstream/base-image packages we don't control), each with an expiry
# to force a revisit rather than a silent permanent exception. Format: one ID per line, optional
# "exp:YYYY-MM-DD" to auto-expire (Trivy 0.73+).
#
# ── packages/persistence/liquibase image (liquibase/liquibase:4.33.0) ───────────────────────
# All entries below found 2026-08-09 via `trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --exit-code 1
# --ignore-unfixed --scanners vuln` against the built migrate image -- see ISSUE-082 for the
# original writeup (filed against the Go stdlib subset before the fuller scan below surfaced the
# rest of this image's bundled Java/OS surface).

# Go stdlib bundled inside Liquibase's own tooling binary (not this project's code; no
# non-breaking fix -- would need Liquibase to publish an image on a patched Go toolchain).
CVE-2025-68121 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2025-61726 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2025-61729 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-25679 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-27145 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-32280 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-32281 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-32283 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-33811 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-33814 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-39820 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-39822 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-39836 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-42499 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-42504 exp:2026-11-01
# Found 2026-08-14 in liquibase/bin/lpm specifically (golang.org/x/net, same bundled-Go-toolchain
# category as the rest of this section).
CVE-2026-39821 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-46600 exp:2026-11-01
# Found 2026-08-15 in liquibase/bin/lpm specifically (Go stdlib itself this time -- asn1,
# net/http, html/template, encoding/xml, net/url, crypto/tls -- same bundled-Go-toolchain
# category as the rest of this section). 90-day revisit window.
CVE-2026-33818 exp:2026-11-13
CVE-2026-56853 exp:2026-11-13
CVE-2026-56858 exp:2026-11-13
CVE-2026-56859 exp:2026-11-13
CVE-2026-56860 exp:2026-11-13
CVE-2026-56862 exp:2026-11-13

# Ubuntu base OS packages (dirmngr, libssl3) inside the liquibase/liquibase:4.33.0 base image --
# not a project dependency; needs an upstream base-image rebuild, not a change here.
CVE-2025-68973 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-45447 exp:2026-11-01

# jackson-databind/jackson-core, bundled by Liquibase itself for its own YAML/JSON changelog
# parsing -- genuinely used by Liquibase internals, not something this project can remove or
# upgrade independently of a new Liquibase release.
CVE-2026-54512 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-54513 exp:2026-11-01
GHSA-r7wm-3cxj-wff9 exp:2026-11-01

# org.postgresql:postgresql, Liquibase's bundled JDBC driver -- genuinely used (this project
# only targets Postgres). No non-breaking fix in the image today; needs a Liquibase release
# bundling a patched driver version.
CVE-2026-42198 exp:2026-11-01
CVE-2026-54291 exp:2026-11-01

# CVE-2025-49146 (pgjdbc insecure auth in channel binding, fixed upstream in 42.7.7): found
# 2026-08-13 against liquibase/liquibase:4.31 (see compose.yaml's LIQUIBASE_IMAGE comment --
# 4.31 is pinned to avoid a separate Pro-license regression in 4.33.0+, which is also the first
# Liquibase release to bundle a patched pgjdbc; no version found that has both fixed at once).
# Low real-world exposure here: only exploitable when a client requires channelBinding=required
# (not configured anywhere in this project), and the migrate container only ever talks to
# Postgres over Docker's private internal network, never anything public. Revisit in 90 days --
# a newer Liquibase minor/patch release may resolve the Pro-license issue without the CVE.
CVE-2025-49146 exp:2026-11-11

# ── apps/web image (nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:mainline-alpine) ────────────────────────────
# libuuid (util-linux), found 2026-09-05 by the same scan against the built web image. The
# advisories name 2.42.3-r0 as the fix, but the Alpine branch this base image pins still publishes
# only 2.42.1-r0 -- confirmed by querying the base image's own index (`apk list libuuid` inside
# nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:mainline-alpine returns 2.42.1-r0 as both installed AND latest).
#
# So there is no build-side change that resolves these. apps/web/Dockerfile already runs
# `apk upgrade --no-cache` for exactly this case; it has nothing to upgrade to. `--ignore-unfixed`
# does not filter them either, because the advisory names a fixed version -- one this base image
# cannot reach. The fix arrives when nginx-unprivileged rebuilds on a newer Alpine.
#
# Deliberately a SHORT window rather than the 2026-11-01 used above: this is expected to resolve
# upstream within weeks, and it should be rechecked then rather than folded into that later batch.
# To recheck: rerun the docker-validate scan, or `apk list libuuid` in the base image -- once it
# offers 2.42.3-r0, delete this whole section rather than extending the date.
CVE-2026-53612 exp:2026-10-03
CVE-2026-53613 exp:2026-10-03
CVE-2026-53614 exp:2026-10-03
CVE-2026-76642 exp:2026-10-03
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2026-10-03
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2026-10-03
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-10-03
